WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.349 --> 00:00:17.576
dad to calm Babu Yadav, but he was still upset.

2
00:00:17.596 --> 00:00:22.340
"He tried to hurt my cow," Babu Yadav said.

3
00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.701
"It is wrong."

4
00:00:25.082 --> 00:00:26.243
"What did I do?"

5
00:00:26.964 --> 00:00:28.465
cried Vinnie, worried.

6
00:00:28.485 --> 00:00:34.795
"Babu Yadav, I give you my word," said Rishi's father.

7
00:00:34.815 --> 00:00:38.157
"I will bring the boy to the king myself."

8
00:00:39.458 --> 00:00:41.320
"You'd better take him to the king!"

9
00:00:41.921 --> 00:00:43.442
Babu Yadav threatened.

10
00:00:44.683 --> 00:00:46.004
He left with the cow.

11
00:00:46.024 --> 00:00:49.507
"Why are cows so important?"

12
00:00:50.108 --> 00:00:50.808
asked Mandy.

13
00:00:50.828 --> 00:00:55.552
"The cow is like our mother," began Rishi's father.

14
00:00:55.572 --> 00:00:59.696
"I don't understand," said Mandy.

15
00:01:00.952 --> 00:01:07.235
"Cows are gentle creatures and provide milk to feed the world," Rishi's father continued.

16
00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:10.096
"It would be wrong to harm your mother."

17
00:01:11.397 --> 00:01:13.037
"Why do I have to see the king?"

18
00:01:13.638 --> 00:01:14.298
asked Vinnie.

19
00:01:14.318 --> 00:01:18.940
"Babu Yadav insists," said Rishi's father.

20
00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:21.801
"We have to go to the palace.

21
00:01:23.002 --> 00:01:24.842
The king will decide what is best."

22
00:01:26.223 --> 00:01:28.344
Rima and her mother stayed home.

23
00:01:29.808 --> 00:01:32.869
Vinnie and Mandy left with Rishi and his father.

24
00:01:34.309 --> 00:01:36.330
They walked down the muddy roads.

25
00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:40.991
Vinnie noticed many cows walking around freely.

26
00:01:42.631 --> 00:01:44.092
"Do you believe in karma?"

27
00:01:44.592 --> 00:01:45.352
asked Rishi.

28
00:01:45.372 --> 00:01:47.453
"What's karma?"

29
00:01:48.013 --> 00:01:48.673
asked Vinnie.

30
00:01:48.693 --> 00:01:52.274
"Our bodies die, but our souls do not.

31
00:01:53.594 --> 00:01:56.155
We live many lives," said Rishi.

32
00:01:56.175 --> 00:02:01.806
"If we hurt an animal or a person, we will be hurt in our next life."

33
00:02:03.187 --> 00:02:07.850
Rishi continued, "This is why all living things should be treated kindly."

34
00:02:09.411 --> 00:02:12.373
Suddenly, they heard a loud clapping noise.

35
00:02:13.494 --> 00:02:16.136
People on the road moved to the side.

36
00:02:17.297 --> 00:02:19.879
Everyone stood still covering their eyes.

37
00:02:19.899 --> 00:02:22.040
"What's up?"

38
00:02:22.561 --> 00:02:23.181
asked Vinnie.

39
00:02:23.201 --> 00:02:25.062
"Do not look!"

40
00:02:25.543 --> 00:02:26.804
Rishi said urgently.

41
00:02:28.312 --> 00:02:31.373
An old man in torn clothes walked up the road.

42
00:02:32.533 --> 00:02:35.094
He was clapping two wooden boards together.

43
00:02:35.114 --> 00:02:39.475
"Hello," Mandy called out to him softly.

44
00:02:40.796 --> 00:02:43.736
The man turned away from Mandy and kept walking.

45
00:02:45.057 --> 00:02:48.918
After he left, Rishi and the others started on their way again.

46
00:02:48.938 --> 00:02:52.439
"Why didn't anyone look at him?"

47
00:02:53.059 --> 00:02:54.359
Mandy asked Rishi.

48
00:02:54.379 --> 00:02:58.377
"He's an untouchable," explained Rishi.

49
00:02:58.397 --> 00:03:01.920
"Why was he clapping those wooden things?"

50
00:03:02.601 --> 00:03:03.221
asked Vinnie.

51
00:03:03.241 --> 00:03:05.223
"It's the law.

52
00:03:05.664 --> 00:03:10.308
Untouchables must alert everyone that they are coming," Rishi replied.

53
00:03:10.328 --> 00:03:13.791
"No one is supposed to even look at them.

54
00:03:15.032 --> 00:03:16.753
They are the lowest kind of people.

55
00:03:18.095 --> 00:03:20.277
Untouchables do the dirtiest jobs."

56
00:03:22.018 --> 00:03:23.920
"Why?" said Mandy.

57
00:03:25.164 --> 00:03:28.666
"We have castes in our society," Rishi began.

58
00:03:29.967 --> 00:03:34.009
He pointed to two men with their hair knotted on top of their heads.

59
00:03:34.029 --> 00:03:37.671
"They are the highest caste, the Brahmans.

60
00:03:38.931 --> 00:03:40.712
They are our religious teachers."

61
00:03:43.354 --> 00:03:47.176
A large elephant with bells came in the opposite direction.

62
00:03:48.316 --> 00:03:51.138
On its back was a colorful rug and carriage.

63
00:03:52.619 --> 00:03:54.920
A young man in white sat on top.

64
00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.459
"The nobles are the next highest caste.

65
00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.221
Like him," said Rishi.

66
00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:05.426
"The next caste is made up of farmers and merchants.

67
00:04:06.687 --> 00:04:10.490
My family belongs to this caste," Rishi said proudly.

68
00:04:10.510 --> 00:04:15.856
"Below us are the servants' caste and finally the untouchables."

69
00:04:17.217 --> 00:04:19.920
Mandy and Vinnie just looked at each other.
